      "thm:lipschitz-all-kappa"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Specialize \\(\\texttt{thm:lipschitz-all-kappa}\\) to \\(\\alpha=1\\) and \\(\\kappa=2\\). Then\n\\[\nr_{n,2}=n^{-2/5},\n\\qquad\n\\epsilon^{2/(2+2)}=\\epsilon^{1/2},\n\\qquad\nV_2(h)=h^{-1}.\n\\]\nConsequently its stochastic term is \\(n^{-1/2}h_n^{-1/2}=(nh_n)^{-1/2}\\), its contamination term is \\(\\epsilon h_n^{-2}\\), and its empty-cell exponent is \\(nh_n^{7/2}\\). Its cellwise contamination and computational bounds specialize verbatim to those in the present statement. This proves the original quadratic-overlap theorem as a corollary and supplies the requested consistency check.",
    "justification": "The original quadratic-overlap result is now a direct corollary of the stronger all-kappa theorem.",
    "gap": "It records the previously solved rate and pre-optimization envelope without competing with the generalized headline.",
    "consumer": "It keeps the quadratic benchmark available for direct comparison with the earlier presolve and applied discussion.",
